        <div class="rh"><span class="mono">The person behind the notes</span><span class="mono">Sheet A</span></div>
        <div class="body">
          <h2 id="ta" class="display h2x" style="font-size: 48px">About &amp; experience.</h2>
          <p class="lead" style="margin-top: 16px">Application Support Engineer in Cardiff, with a background in customer-facing technology, automation and analysis, and a habit of putting sensors on things.</p>
          <aside class="mn"><span class="mono">Elsewhere</span><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/julianelliott/">LinkedIn</a> for dates and detail · <a href="https://github.com/Julian-Elliott">GitHub</a> for the code · <a href="https://databased.business/">databased.business</a> for the datasets · <a href="mailto:julianpaulelliott@icloud.com">email</a> for an interesting problem.</aside>
          <p>I work on the systems that credit and receivables businesses run on: SQL-based data fixes, Oracle and PostgreSQL, triage, root cause, and the explaining that follows. Before that, John Lewis: eleven years across technology sales, customer delivery resolution and automation, where the questions were the same and the tools were different.</p>
          <div class="career"><div class="when">Now</div><div><h3>Application Support Engineer</h3><p>Cardiff · Making systems easier to understand, use and fix; the thread running through this notebook.</p></div></div>
          <div class="career"><div class="when">2021–2024</div><div><h3>Automation Senior Analyst</h3><p>John Lewis Partnership · Automation, dashboards and mentoring, with an eye on the work people needed to get done.</p></div></div>
          <div class="career"><div class="when">2020–2021</div><div><h3>Customer Delivery Resolution Partner</h3><p>John Lewis Partnership · Resolving operational problems and improving the process around them.</p></div></div>
          <div class="career"><div class="when">2013–2020</div><div><h3>Technology Selling Partner</h3><p>John Lewis Partnership · Helping customers understand technology and sharing product knowledge with colleagues.</p></div></div>
          <div class="career"><div class="when">2024–2026</div><div><h3>MSc Data Analytics</h3><p>University of Huddersfield · Dissertation in progress: domestic heating data from metered dwellings.</p></div></div>
          <h3 class="h2">Away from the screen.</h3>
          <p>I climb, walk along canals, grow vegetables and make things: 3D printing, electronics, furniture, a guitar now and then. Some of those things eventually acquire a circuit board. Others are just a good way to spend an afternoon.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf"><a class="mono" href="#sheet-01">← Contents</a><a class="mono" href="mailto:julianpaulelliott@icloud.com">Say hello →</a></div>
